Talmak spots the line and heaves a slab of solid rock from the dirt to bar my path. I slash the curved blade into the rock, but the edge catches and binds in the stone. The mineral density has been magically hardened, dense as Kate's reinforced frost.

Without maxed strength and toughness to punch through stone, my arm would shatter on impact. I yank the scimitar free and bank wide around the barrier, hunting another seam.

}
#if(v_strength == 4 && v_toughness == 4 && v_b2_ch5_scimitar != 0) {
 

Crossbow bolts won't bite through the layered physical wards wrapping Talmak's frame. Close quarters with steel is the only angle.

As the bodyguards peel off to intercept Daren, Kate, and Leila, I throw my arms up. The air currents grip me, launching me straight at the sage with my scimitar drawn.

Talmak spots the line and heaves a slab of solid rock from the dirt to bar my path. I slash the curved blade into the rock, but the edge catches and binds in the stone. The mineral density has been magically hardened, dense as Kate's reinforced frost.

I wrench the scimitar free, drop it into the scabbard, and drive my boosted fist straight through the center of the slab, shattering it to dust just like Hadrik.

}
#if(v_toughness < 4) {
 "Hah!" Hadrik barks. "I was hoping that you'd be coming this way, Barry. Let's see if you can keep up!"

He ramps his tempo, fists pounding into stone barriers while I dive from above. Talmak throws his palms outward, detonating a concussive shockwave of compressed air that flings us both backward. A stone platform materializes beneath his boots, carrying him fifty feet into the sky.

"So he handles air too..." Hadrik grunts, rolling to his feet. "Bastard. Come on, Barry, let's catch up to him!"

I drive upward on the drafts as Hadrik morphs into a giant eagle, broad wings beating the air beside me. Just as we close on the platform, two massive rock slabs manifest above and below me, snapping shut like an iron vice.

The stone plates collide with crushing force, pulverizing my body instantly before everything goes dark.

}
#if(v_toughness == 4 && v_strength < 4) {
 "Hah!" Hadrik barks. "I was hoping that you'd be coming this way, Barry. Let's see if you can keep up!"

He ramps his tempo, fists pounding into stone barriers while I dive from above. Talmak throws his palms outward, detonating a concussive shockwave of compressed air that flings us both backward. A stone platform materializes beneath his boots, carrying him fifty feet into the sky.

"So he handles air too..." Hadrik grunts, rolling to his feet. "Bastard. Come on, Barry, let's catch up to him!"

I drive upward on the drafts as Hadrik morphs into a giant eagle, broad wings beating the air beside me. Just as we close on the platform, two massive rock slabs manifest above and below me, snapping shut like an iron vice.

My maxed toughness keeps my ribcage from caving immediately, but the slabs clamp tight. I strain against the stone, but without the physical strength to force them open, I'm pinned cold. Talmak manifests two more heavy blocks and slams them into the press with full force, crushing me flat.

}
#if(v_strength == 4 && v_toughness == 4) {
 "Hah!" Hadrik barks. "I was hoping that you'd be coming this way, Barry. Let's see if you can keep up!"

He ramps his tempo, fists pounding into stone barriers while I dive from above. Talmak throws his palms outward, detonating a concussive shockwave of compressed air that flings us both backward. A stone platform materializes beneath his boots, carrying him fifty feet into the sky.

"So he handles air too..." Hadrik grunts, rolling to his feet. "Bastard. Come on, Barry, let's catch up to him!"

I drive upward on the drafts as Hadrik morphs into a giant eagle, broad wings beating the air beside me. Just as we close on the platform, two massive rock slabs manifest above and below me, snapping shut like an iron vice.

The slabs slam together, trapping me between two tons of rock. I brace my left forearm against the upper plate and hammer my right fist straight into the stone before me. The slab explodes in a burst of gravel, and I shoot through the gap into open air, resuming the climb toward Talmak as he tries the same crushing tactic on Hadrik.

}
