ID: B2-Ch10b-Trouble
TEXT:

 Hadrik struggles against the airborne slabs. Shifting into an eagle costs him mass and natural resilience; even his aura-hardening trick can't fully shield avian bones against multi-ton crushing blocks. Every time Talmak sandwiches him between stone plates, Hadrik has to drop the bird shape, revert to dwarf form mid-air to smash his way clear, and lose all his upward momentum.

Punching through individual blocks buys me inches, but Talmak's casting rate is relentless. Down in the yard, jagged boulders ripped straight from the bedrock begin hurtling upward. Shattering everything by hand is a losing game; I need a tactical pivot.

choice("Try to use the sage's own techniques against him", B2-Ch10b-Technique, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10b-Technique, v_b2_ch10_tactic = 0)
choice("Rely on my reaction speed to dodge the rocks until I reach Talmak", B2-Ch10b-Reaction, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10b-Reaction, v_b2_ch10_tactic = 1)
choice("Try to obtain the advantage by being more aware of my surroundings", B2-Ch10b-Observe, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10b-Observe, v_b2_ch10_tactic = 2)


ID: B2-Ch10b-Technique
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_combat_technique < 4)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_combat_technique == 4)
 

Time to turn the field.

The ground-torn boulders rise slower than the conjured stone, their flight paths wobbling slightly. Raw earth requires less mana than shaping matter from nothing, but Talmak's telekinetic grip on it is coarser. That gap is usable.

I punch through the conjured slabs in front of me while weaving around the natural boulders, letting each near-miss swing around into my slipstream. Within thirty seconds, half a dozen heavy rocks are chasing my tail, pulled along in a tight formation. Talmak is busy keeping Hadrik suppressed and hasn't registered the buildup.

The moment his focus locks on Hadrik's latest dive, I plunge straight down toward the sage's platform.

#if(v_combat_technique < 4) {
 Talmak glances up a fraction too early. A massive stone slate snaps into existence directly in my dive path. I brake hard, but the trailing boulders behind me have too much inertia; they slam into my back at full velocity, grinding me against the slate.

}
#if(v_combat_technique == 4) {
 The trailing boulders stay locked on my tail. I hold the dive until the platform fills my vision, then snap my air currents into a sharp lateral roll at the last possible fraction of a second.

Talmak doesn't even look up before the entire swarm of boulders hammers into his platform like siege artillery.

He manages a frantic dome of stone around himself, absorbing the worst of the impact, but the platform fractures into rubble. The whole structure collapses, sending Talmak tumbling through the debris.

He conjures a replacement slab twenty feet lower, blowing the dust clear with a burst of wind, his face dark with fury.

"He's looking pretty pissed, Barry," Hadrik calls out, hovering nearby on eagle wings. "You think you can handle him, while I go get Daren? He's the one that specializes against elementalists, after all. Aerial battles are just not my thing."

"Yeah, go get him," I say. "Make it fast. I can't dance up here forever."

Hadrik dives for the ground. Talmak ignores the eagle entirely, gliding his new platform back up to my altitude.

He starts hurling stones with both hands, rapid-fire, but the rage is bleeding into his technique; the volleys are wilder, drifting off-target.

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_combat_technique < 4)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_combat_technique < 4)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_combat_technique < 4)
choice("Continue", B2-Ch10b-Mosquito, v_ac_b2_ch10_demolition = 1, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10b-Mosquito) if (v_combat_technique == 4)


ID: B2-Ch10b-Reaction
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_reflexes < 4)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_reflexes == 4)
#if(v_reflexes < 4) {
 

Stop playing defense. Checking every single incoming stone slows the advance to a crawl; getting to Talmak means pushing the margins.

I drop the wide sweeps and drive hard for the platform, dodging only at the point of contact.

The sheer volume of fire proves too dense. A stray boulder catches me on the temple, spinning me out of control. Before my senses clear, two stone slabs slam shut over me, ending it instantly.

}
#if(v_reflexes == 4) {
 

Stop playing defense. Checking every single incoming stone slows the advance to a crawl; getting to Talmak means pushing the margins.

I drop the wide sweeps and drive hard for the platform, cutting through the barrage with split-second twitch dodges.

The reckless line closes the gap in seconds. While Talmak is tracking Hadrik's descent, I slip past his peripheral guard, plant my feet on the edge of his stone slab, and bury a boosted right cross into his jaw.

His defensive enchantments absorb the lethal force, saving him from a fractured skull, but the impact blows him clean off the platform with a bloody nose. He plummets thirty feet before conjuring another slab beneath his boots, his face dark with fury.

"He's looking pretty pissed, Barry," Hadrik calls out, hovering nearby on eagle wings. "You think you can handle him, while I go get Daren? He's the one that specializes against elementalists, after all. Aerial battles are just not my thing."

"Yeah, go get him," I say. "Make it fast. I can't dance up here forever."

Hadrik dives for the ground. Talmak ignores the eagle entirely, gliding his new platform back up to my altitude.

He starts hurling stones with both hands, rapid-fire, but the rage is bleeding into his technique; the volleys are wilder, drifting off-target.

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_reflexes < 4)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_reflexes < 4)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_reflexes < 4)
choice("Continue", B2-Ch10b-Mosquito, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10b-Mosquito) if (v_reflexes == 4)


ID: B2-Ch10b-Observe
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_perception < 4)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_perception == 4)
 

Time to analyze the field.

I map the airborne clutter in my head—every rising boulder, every hovering slab—tracking trajectories and blind spots.

Talmak casts on predictive lines, setting obstacles where he expects a target to head. Erratic, non-linear flight paths will force him to waste mana conjuring barriers in empty air, leaving him dependent on the slower earth-torn boulders.

I break into irregular, jagged loops, constantly breaking rhythm. The conjured slabs miss wide, but I still need to exploit his recovery window.

#if(v_perception < 4) {
 Tunneling on Talmak's hand gestures blinds me to the natural boulders rising from below. A heavy stone catches me in the side of the head, and before I can recover my balance, two slabs crush me flat.

}
#if(v_perception == 4) {
 The pattern reveals itself: every time Talmak redirects a boulder, his posture stiffens for half a second, telegraphing his focus.

I feint right, draw a misplaced slab, and cut into his blind spot while he turns to intercept Hadrik. Dropping onto his floating platform, I drive a boosted fist into his jaw before he can turn.

His enchantments keep his skull in one piece, but the blow knocks him backward off the edge, blood leaking from his nose. He halts his fall on a freshly conjured slab thirty feet below, glaring up in pure rage.

"He's looking pretty pissed, Barry," Hadrik calls out, hovering nearby on eagle wings. "You think you can handle him, while I go get Daren? He's the one that specializes against elementalists, after all. Aerial battles are just not my thing."

"Yeah, go get him," I say. "Make it fast. I can't dance up here forever."

Hadrik dives for the ground. Talmak ignores the eagle entirely, gliding his new platform back up to my altitude.

He starts hurling stones with both hands, rapid-fire, but the rage is bleeding into his technique; the volleys are wilder, drifting off-target.

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_perception < 4)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_perception < 4)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_perception < 4)
choice("Continue", B2-Ch10b-Mosquito, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10b-Mosquito) if (v_perception == 4)


ID: B2-Ch10b-Mosquito
TEXT:

achievement("Demolition man",v_ac_b2_ch10_demolition)
 "Stop flying around like a damn mosquito!" Talmak roars, hurling another heavy boulder that whistles past my shoulder.

"Can't help it," I shout back. "Piloting habits die hard, and aerial magic handles about the same. Bad luck for you!"

"I am going to enjoy cracking that neck of yours, boy!" Talmak launches three rocks in tight succession; I bank hard left, letting the stones tear through empty air.

"Come on," I taunt. "Every low-rent mercenary in the arena had better lines than that. Is that the best a sage can do?"

Banking wide over the compound, I track the ground battle. Daren is locked in a brutal exchange of steel with Nolderan when Hadrik drops from the sky, shedding his eagle form the instant his boots hit the dirt.

Hadrik doesn't hesitate. He drives a boosted sprint into Nolderan's flank, planting a massive punch into the ex-sage's ribs that hurls him twenty feet into the stone perimeter wall. Hadrik yells something to Daren, points up toward my dogfight, and steps into Nolderan's path. Daren throws up a flare of white healing light over his bruised sword-arm and breaks into a run.

On the other side of the yard, Kate and Leila are trading fire with the two scarred dwarf bodyguards behind an ice wall, while the blond elf snaps floating kinetic barriers into position to deflect Kate's frost volleys. Higher up, the dark-haired banshee is circling Illuna in a blinding duel of elemental spells.

Melindra remains secure in the golden cage; Illuna must have used her daily teleportation spell to slip through the bars and join the fight.

The enemy banshee fights as a true generalist—chaining lightning, fire streams, sonic blasts, and ice cones in rapid succession, supported by summoned raptors harrying Illuna's flanks. With Talmak's rocks whistling around my ears, I don't have time to analyze the full exchange.

I lead Talmak through two more spiraling loops until Daren's voice thunders from below.

"Talmak!" Daren bellows, sword raised high. "Get down here and face me! What kind of coward hides behind altitude where steel can't reach him?"

"Watch your tongue, healer in armor!" Talmak snarls from his platform. "Who do you think you're talking to?"

"He has a point," I yell down, making sure my voice carries. "Strongest earth elementalist alive, right? Why the aerial parlor tricks? You don't get floating platforms in the yearly sage duels. What's the matter—afraid of Daren?"

"What did you say?..." Talmak's head snaps toward me.

"He's asking if you're afraid of me, Talmak!" Daren shouts. "Answer the man!"

"You'll choke on that insolence, healer!" Talmak roars. "I don't care what fairy tales they tell about your sword. I'll grind you into the bedrock!"

He drops the platform in a steep plunge, slamming it onto the dirt with a shuddering crash. He steps off onto the ground, earth magic already churning around his boots.

I ease my air currents and touch down twenty paces away to keep eyes on the clash.

choice("Continue", B2-Ch10b-Intensely, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10b-Intensely)


ID: B2-Ch10b-Henchmen
TEXT:

#if(v_b2_ch5_scimitar != 0) {
 I shoulder the crossbow and snap three quick bolts at the advancing bodyguards. The iron tips strike invisible defensive wards inches from their chests and ricochet away with dull metallic clinks. Talmak pre-cast physical shielding over his entire squad. I sling the crossbow across my back and draw my scimitar.

Talmak hammers Hadrik back with a hurled boulder and rides his rising stone slab into the sky. Hadrik rolls with the impact, morphs into a giant eagle on the bounce, and drives his wings hard to give chase.

Nolderan leads the squad's charge, heading straight for Daren. Steel meets steel in a shower of sparks, and before the other four can flank them, Kate raises a thick dome of reinforced ice over Leila, me, and herself. A split second later, twin jets of roaring flame from the two dwarf bodyguards wash over the frost shell, hissing into steam.

"Hold your fire!" the dark-haired banshee barks over the roar of the flames. "I need answers from that amulet!"

"To hell with your questions, abomination!" the eyepatch dwarf spits, keeping his hands forward as fire pours from his palms. "The master gave you a leash. Don't presume to command us!"

}
#if(v_b2_ch5_scimitar == 0) {
 I shoulder the crossbow and snap three quick bolts at the advancing bodyguards. The iron tips strike invisible defensive wards inches from their chests and ricochet away with dull metallic clinks. Talmak pre-cast physical shielding over his entire squad. I sling the crossbow across my back and draw my dagger.

Talmak hammers Hadrik back with a hurled boulder and rides his rising stone slab into the sky. Hadrik rolls with the impact, morphs into a giant eagle on the bounce, and drives his wings hard to give chase.

Nolderan leads the squad's charge, heading straight for Daren. Steel meets steel in a shower of sparks, and before the other four can flank them, Kate raises a thick dome of reinforced ice over Leila, me, and herself. A split second later, twin jets of roaring flame from the two dwarf bodyguards wash over the frost shell, hissing into steam.

"Hold your fire!" the dark-haired banshee barks over the roar of the flames. "I need answers from that amulet!"

"To hell with your questions, abomination!" the eyepatch dwarf spits, keeping his hands forward as fire pours from his palms. "The master gave you a leash. Don't presume to command us!"

}
 "The sage is no master of mine," the banshee retorts, green eyes flaring. "We have a contract. I secure his Magium claim; he registers me for the tournament so I can hunt what I came for."

"Talmak letting you breathe is charity enough," the scarred dwarf snarls. "I'd have purged you at the gate."

Kate doesn't wait for them to finish. A volley of a hundred frost daggers forms above the compound and plunges toward the squad.

The icicles strike an invisible barrier surrounding the four mages and shatter into powder. Nolderan, outside the ward, weaves through the falling frost with practiced martial footwork, parrying Daren's counter-thrust without breaking stride.

"Could we perhaps table the faction squabbling?" the blond elf says, maintaining a strained, tight smile as he channels the barrier. "Had I not cast this ward, you would both be impaled on the dirt."

"I saw the cast," the banshee snaps. "I was already moving."

"Is that why you stood completely still?" the elf's smile twitches.

"Shut up," she seethes. "Drop the barrier and let me speak!"

"By all means," the elf says. "Ask your question so we can get back to killing them."

The banshee steps toward our ice dome, emerald light blazing in her eyes. "You in the ice! What is the name of the spirit bound to that amulet?"

choice("Continue", B2-Ch10b-Henchmen2, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10b-Henchmen2)


ID: B2-Ch10b-Henchmen2
TEXT:

 "What makes you think that we'll answer your question?" Kate calls through the frost.

"Answer, and I make your deaths quick," the banshee says. "Refuse, and—"

A volley of roaring fireballs cascades from the sky, detonating across the squad's position in a deafening thunderclap.

"Arraka," Illuna's cold voice rings out from above. "Her name is Arraka."

Illuna hovers twelve feet up on Flower's fire jets, blue light radiating from her pupils.

"How did you get out of the cage?" I ask.

"The creator of the golden cage can teleport through its lattice," Illuna says. "The design allows escape if an enemy is trapped inside by mistake. I rarely expend my daily teleportation spell, so the charge was ready."

"And Melindra?"

"Conscious and stabilizing," Illuna says. "The healing weave requires several minutes to knit the bone. I extended the cage's duration to hold her safe, though the mana cost was steep."

"Are you done exchanging notes?" the enemy banshee calls up, stepping through the clearing smoke.

The elf's barrier absorbed the entire fireball volley without a scratch, its dense kinetic aura shimmering faintly in the air.

"Nobody asked you to wait," Illuna says flatly. "Attack whenever you wish."

"I would have gutted you already," the eyepatch dwarf growls, "if this idiot hadn't wrapped us in a two-way barrier that blocks our own spells!"

"I lower the ward when our banshee finishes," the elf replies smoothly. "And when you demonstrate you can survive ten seconds of combat without needing me to wipe your noses."

The dark-haired banshee ignores them both, fixing her gaze on Flower's amulet. "The spirit in the gold casing... How old is she? Has she walked the realms for a thousand years? Five thousand?"

"Try quite a bit longer than five millennia, little girl," Arraka's mocking voice rings from the metal. "Stop dancing around it. What do you want?"

"Then answer me plainly," the banshee says, her aura darkening with ancient fury. "Did you, or did you not cause the banishment of all female spirits from the magical plane five thousand years ago?"

choice("Continue", B2-Ch10b-Henchmen3, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10b-Henchmen3)


ID: B2-Ch10b-Henchmen3
TEXT:

 "Ahahahahaha!" Arraka's laughter shrills from the amulet. "There are still banshees who remember? Centuries sealed under a mountain and the legend still has teeth! You have no idea how proud I am right now!"

"So it is true..." The woman's fists shake, green flame flickering at her fingertips. "The rumors were real. The only reason I entered this tournament was to follow the trace of your aura. Millennia of exile, forced into parasitic host bodies... all because of your slaughter!"

"And what are you going to do about it?" Arraka taunts.

"I am going to end you!" the banshee screams. "I will avenge every soul cursed to this existence!"

"Destroying the amulet only breaks her seal," Illuna warns coldly. "You will free her, and doom us all."

"Then I will kill her in the flesh!" the banshee roars. "Again and again until nothing remains! Drop the ward, elf! Drop it now!"

"Gladly," the elf says, dismissing the kinetic field. "Try not to die immediately."

The two dwarves instantly link their mana, unleashing a concentrated beam of white-hot flame against Kate's ice dome. Frost melts into scalding steam under the heat; Kate braces her boots, reinforcing the inner layer as fast as it vaporizes, but the strain shows in her jaw.

The black-haired banshee launches skyward, engaging Illuna in an aerial duel.

She fights as a versatile generalist, chaining lightning arcs, concussive sonic blasts, and freezing beams in rapid succession while directing summoned raptors to flank Illuna's blind spots. Flower's aerial maneuvers keep them clear of lethal hits, but neither side can land a clean blow.

Kate sends a spread of icicles toward the dwarves, but flat kinetic shields snap into place mid-air, deflecting every projectile. The elf offers a mocking salute from behind his ward.

Kate scowls, turning to Leila and me inside the melting dome.

"If either of you could keep some of those three mages busy, while I attack them, it would be highly appreciated..."

choice("Run towards the mages, and focus on attacking the elf", B2-Ch10b-Run-elf, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10b-Run-elf)
choice("Run towards the mages, and focus on attacking the dwarves", B2-Ch10b-Run-dwarves, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10b-Run-dwarves)
choice("Fly towards the mages, and focus on attacking the elf ", B2-Ch10b-Fly-elf, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10b-Fly-elf)
choice("Fly towards the mages, and focus on attacking the dwarves", B2-Ch10b-Fly-dwarves, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10b-Fly-dwarves)


ID: B2-Ch10b-Run-dwarves
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_agility < 3 || v_reflexes < 3)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_agility >= 3 && v_reflexes >= 3)
#if(v_agility < 3) {
 

"I'm on it," Leila writes.

"Me too," I say. "Open the dome."

Kate flicks her fingers outward, parting a shoulder-width slit in the frost wall.

"We take the dwarves first," I whisper to Leila. "Heavy offense, light defense, and the elf can't cover three angles at once. Pincer them. I'll break left."

Leila nods. We slip through the opening, and Kate seals the ice behind our heels. Leila sprints right across the yard as I peel left. The two fire mages spot the split instantly, the scarred dwarf turning his flames toward Leila while the eyepatch dwarf pivots on me.

I cut hard to dodge the incoming fire stream and slam full-tilt into an invisible kinetic barrier. The collision stops me dead; before I can scramble back, a column of white-hot flame engulfs me, incinerating me where I stand.

}
#if(v_agility >= 3 && v_reflexes < 3) {
 

"I'm on it," Leila writes.

"Me too," I say. "Open the dome."

Kate flicks her fingers outward, parting a shoulder-width slit in the frost wall.

"We take the dwarves first," I whisper to Leila. "Heavy offense, light defense, and the elf can't cover three angles at once. Pincer them. I'll break left."

Leila nods. We slip through the opening, and Kate seals the ice behind our heels. Leila sprints right across the yard as I peel left. The two fire mages spot the split instantly, the scarred dwarf turning his flames toward Leila while the eyepatch dwarf pivots on me.

I dodge the first blast of flame, weaving around the elf's invisible barrier placements with boosted agility. The kinetic shields limit our approach angles, but the elf struggles to track our speed while managing two separate targets.

A sudden shriek of frost cuts through the air. Kate launches dozens of icicles from three directions straight at the elf's flank, forcing him to drop his perimeter wards and snap a personal kinetic sphere around himself.

The dwarves are left exposed, but as we close the final yards, both mages thrust their palms forward, discharging point-blank fire jets.

Leila drops into a low slide with superhuman reflexes, clearing the blast. My reaction time is a fraction too slow; the fire catches me in the chest, killing me instantly.

}
#if(v_agility >= 3 && v_reflexes >= 3) {
 

"I'm on it," Leila writes.

"Me too," I say. "Open the dome."

Kate flicks her fingers outward, parting a shoulder-width slit in the frost wall.

"We take the dwarves first," I whisper to Leila. "Heavy offense, light defense, and the elf can't cover three angles at once. Pincer them. I'll break left."

Leila nods. We slip through the opening, and Kate seals the ice behind our heels. Leila sprints right across the yard as I peel left. The two fire mages spot the split instantly, the scarred dwarf turning his flames toward Leila while the eyepatch dwarf pivots on me.

I dodge the first blast of flame, weaving around the elf's invisible barrier placements with boosted agility. The kinetic shields limit our approach angles, but the elf struggles to track our speed while managing two separate targets.

A sudden shriek of frost cuts through the air. Kate launches dozens of icicles from three directions straight at the elf's flank, forcing him to drop his perimeter wards and snap a personal kinetic sphere around himself.

The dwarves are left exposed, thrusting their palms forward to discharge point-blank fire jets.

Leila slides beneath the blast; I twist aside on pure reflex, ducking under the scorching cone of heat. Before the dwarves can reset their stances, our blades slash across their throats, slicing cleanly through their physical wards and dropping both bodies into the dirt.

"So much for the great sage's elite squad, eh?" I turn toward the elf, blade dripping.

"Easily replaced pawns," the elf says with a strained, tight smile. "The senior squad is securing the pinecone harvest. You will not survive long enough to meet them; the sage will grind you to dust."

"The sage?" I ask, stepping closer. "Not you?"

"I handle defense," he replies smoothly. "No offensive repertoire to speak of. I intend to hold this sphere until you exhaust yourselves or lose interest. You cannot pierce it."

"Right..." Leila and I begin hammering rapid strikes into the kinetic sphere.

Above us, Talmak continues driving Hadrik's eagle across the sky with hurled boulders; Hadrik keeps having to revert to dwarf form mid-air to shatter the larger rocks. Lower down, Illuna and Flower remain locked in a dead heat with the enemy banshee, trading blasts across the open air.

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_agility < 3 || v_reflexes < 3)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_agility < 3 || v_reflexes < 3)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_agility < 3 || v_reflexes < 3)
choice("Continue", B2-Ch10b-Specialty, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10b-Specialty) if (v_agility >= 3 && v_reflexes >= 3)


ID: B2-Ch10b-Fly-dwarves
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_reflexes < 3)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_reflexes >= 3)
 

"I'm on it," Leila writes.

"Me too," I say. "Open the dome."

Kate flicks her fingers outward, parting a shoulder-width slit in the frost wall.

"We take the dwarves first," I tell Leila. "Heavy offense, light defense, and the elf can't cover three angles at once. I'll strike from above; you hit them on the ground."

Leila nods. We clear the dome, and Kate seals the ice behind us. Leila sprints across the dirt while I throw my arms up, riding the air currents skyward. The two dwarves switch focus immediately, the scarred dwarf tracking Leila with fireballs while the eyepatch dwarf directs a column of flame upward at me.

I bank through the fire stream and dive on the dwarf's blind spot, but a flat semi-transparent barrier snaps into my trajectory. I bank hard to clear the edge, but the ward tracks my line, blocking every angle until another blast of fire forces me to pull up.

#if(v_reflexes < 3) {
 On the ground, Leila struggles against invisible kinetic shields. I commit to a second dive, but another barrier cuts off the angle.

A shriek of frost fills the air as Kate launches dozens of icicles straight at the elf, forcing him to drop his distant shields and wrap himself in a personal kinetic sphere.

The dwarves lose their cover, but as Leila and I close the distance, both mages thrust their palms forward, discharging point-blank fire jets.

Leila slides under the flames on reflex. My reaction time is a fraction too slow; the fire catches me full-on, incinerating me instantly.

}
#if(v_reflexes >= 3) {
 On the ground, Leila struggles against invisible kinetic shields. I commit to a second dive, but another barrier cuts off the angle.

A shriek of frost fills the air as Kate launches dozens of icicles straight at the elf, forcing him to drop his distant shields and wrap himself in a personal kinetic sphere.

The dwarves lose their cover, thrusting their palms forward to unleash point-blank fire jets.

Leila slides beneath the blast; I drop out of my dive and twist aside on pure reflex, evading the scorching cone of heat. Before the dwarves can reset their stances, our blades slash across their throats, slicing cleanly through their physical wards and dropping both bodies into the dirt.

"So much for the great sage's elite squad, eh?" I touch down beside the corpses and advance on the elf.

"Easily replaced pawns," the elf says with a strained, tight smile. "The senior squad is securing the pinecone harvest. You will not survive long enough to meet them; the sage will grind you to dust."

"The sage?" I ask. "Not you?"

"I handle defense," he replies smoothly. "No offensive repertoire to speak of. I intend to hold this sphere until you exhaust yourselves or lose interest. You cannot pierce it."

"Right..." Leila and I begin hammering rapid strikes into the kinetic sphere.

Above us, Talmak continues driving Hadrik's eagle across the sky with hurled boulders; Hadrik keeps having to revert to dwarf form mid-air to shatter the larger rocks. Lower down, Illuna and Flower remain locked in a dead heat with the enemy banshee, trading blasts across the open air.

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_reflexes < 3)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_reflexes < 3)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_reflexes < 3)
choice("Continue", B2-Ch10b-Specialty, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10b-Specialty) if (v_reflexes >= 3)


ID: B2-Ch10b-Run-elf
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_agility < 3)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_agility >= 3)
#if(v_agility < 3) {
 

"I'm on it," Leila writes.

"Me too," I say. "Open the dome."

Kate flicks her fingers outward, parting a shoulder-width slit in the frost wall.

"Target the elf first," I whisper to Leila. "Pressure him together and force him to turtle behind his own shield. Without his barriers, Kate can skewer the dwarves. Pincer him. I'll break left."

Leila nods. We slip through the opening, and Kate seals the ice behind our heels. Leila sprints right while I take the left flank. The two fire mages spot the split instantly, directing flame streams to cut off our advance.

I cut hard to dodge the incoming fire and slam full-tilt into an invisible kinetic barrier. The collision stops me dead; before I can scramble back, a column of white-hot flame engulfs me, incinerating me where I stand.

}
#if(v_agility >= 3) {
 

"I'm on it," Leila writes.

"Me too," I say. "Open the dome."

Kate flicks her fingers outward, parting a shoulder-width slit in the frost wall.

"Target the elf first," I whisper to Leila. "Pressure him together and force him to turtle behind his own shield. Without his barriers, Kate can skewer the dwarves. Pincer him. I'll break left."

Leila nods. We slip through the opening, and Kate seals the ice behind our heels. Leila sprints right while I take the left flank. The two fire mages spot the split instantly, directing flame streams to cut off our advance.

I dodge the first blast of flame, weaving around the elf's invisible barrier placements with boosted agility. He scrambles to position shields between us, but the pincer stretches his concentration thin.

A sudden shriek of frost cuts through the air. Kate launches dozens of icicles straight at the elf's flank, forcing him to drop all perimeter wards and snap a personal kinetic sphere around himself.

Leila and I close in instantly, pinning him beneath a barrage of blade strikes. With the elf stripped of his area defense, Kate drives twin heavy icicles through the skulls of both fire mages, dropping them instantly.

"So much for the great sage's elite squad, eh?" I keep hammering the elf's kinetic sphere alongside Leila.

"Easily replaced pawns," the elf says with a strained, tight smile. "The senior squad is securing the pinecone harvest. You will not survive long enough to meet them; the sage will grind you to dust."

"The sage?" I ask. "Not you?"

"I handle defense," he replies smoothly. "No offensive repertoire to speak of. I intend to hold this sphere until you exhaust yourselves or lose interest. You cannot pierce it."

"Right..." I keep the pressure on with steel.

Above us, Talmak continues driving Hadrik's eagle across the sky with hurled boulders; Hadrik keeps having to revert to dwarf form mid-air to shatter the larger rocks. Lower down, Illuna and Flower remain locked in a dead heat with the enemy banshee, trading blasts across the open air.

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_agility < 3)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_agility < 3)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_agility < 3)
choice("Continue", B2-Ch10b-Specialty, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10b-Specialty) if (v_agility >= 3)


