Above us, Talmak continues driving Hadrik's eagle across the sky with hurled boulders; Hadrik keeps having to revert to dwarf form mid-air to shatter the larger rocks. Lower down, Illuna and Flower remain locked in a dead heat with the enemy banshee, trading blasts across the open air.

choice("Continue", B2-Ch10b-Specialty, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10b-Specialty)


ID: B2-Ch10b-Specialty
TEXT:

 Across the yard, Daren's duel with Nolderan is tipping into dangerous territory. Nolderan hasn't taken a scratch, his enchanted blade slipping through Daren's guard to bite at an unarmored elbow seam. Daren's movements are slowing, dark blood staining his tunic under the plate.

Before I can disengage to assist, Hadrik drops out of the sky in eagle form, shedding the feathers the instant his boots hit the dirt. Talmak hovers high above on his rock slab, boulder swarm suspended around him, waiting on Hadrik's next climb.

"Yield, Daren," Nolderan says, pressing his blade against Daren's parry. "You've picked up some tricks, but you cannot match my form. Beg Sage Talmak for mercy, and he might still spare your--"

Hadrik's boosted sprint hits Nolderan from the blind side like a battering ram, a massive right fist blasting the ex-sage twenty feet into the stone perimeter wall.

"Team fight, old man, not an exhibition duel," Hadrik grins. "Check your flanks next time."

"Noted," Nolderan grunts, pushing himself up from the rubble.

"I'll deal with your old master," Hadrik tells Daren, waving him off. "Go ground the sage. Elementalists are your specialty, aren't they?"

"They are," Daren says. White healing light washes over his bruised arm, knitting the cut. "I'll handle him."

"Good!" Hadrik turns on Nolderan. "Come on, old man, let's see some real footwork!"

Hadrik lunges forward, but Nolderan sways beneath the punch with veteran precision, stepping into a counter.

Daren turns his back on the clash and roars at the sky.

"Talmak!" Daren bellows, raising his glowing broadsword. "Get down here and face me! What kind of coward hides behind altitude where steel can't reach him?"

"Watch your tongue, healer in armor!" Talmak snarls from his platform. "Who do you think you're talking to?"

"He has a point," I yell up, making sure my voice carries. "Strongest earth elementalist alive, right? Why the aerial parlor tricks? You don't get floating platforms in the yearly sage duels. What's the matter—afraid of Daren?"

"What did you say?..." Talmak's head snaps toward me.

"He's asking if you're afraid of me, Talmak!" Daren shouts. "Answer the man!"

"You'll choke on that insolence, healer!" Talmak roars. "I don't care what fairy tales they tell about your sword. I'll grind you into the bedrock!"

He drops the platform in a steep plunge, slamming it onto the dirt with a shuddering crash. He steps off onto the ground, earth magic already churning around his boots as Daren's healing weave settles.

choice("Continue", B2-Ch10b-Intensely, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10b-Intensely)


ID: B2-Ch10b-Intensely
TEXT:

 Talmak halts thirty yards out, boots planted wide, eyes locked on Daren.

The yard falls still around them. Hadrik and Nolderan step back from their grapple; the elf holds his barrier; Kate and Leila hold their stances. The only sound left in the compound is the whistling roar of Flower and the dark-haired banshee circling each other high above.

choice("Cheer for Daren", B2-Ch10b-Cheer, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10b-Cheer)
choice("Insult the sage", B2-Ch10b-Insult, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10b-Insult)
choice("Stay silent and watch the fight", B2-Ch10b-Silent, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10b-Silent)


ID: B2-Ch10b-Cheer
TEXT:

 "You can do it, Daren!" I shout. "If you win this fight, they will be writing stories of you for many more years to come!"

"This is going to be his last story, boy," Talmak sneers. "I'm going to make sure of it."

Talmak thrusts both hands forward. Two massive boulders, each twice Daren's height, tear through the air with concussive force.

Daren doesn't flinch. He steps into the line and sweeps his broadsword in a single, fluid arc through the center of both projectiles.

The blade glides through the stone like butter. Instead of shattering, the magical rock collapses inward, shrinking in seconds until two smooth stone marbles orbit the enchanted steel, locked in its gravitational pull.

"What?..." Talmak's jaw drops. "No, this can't be..."

He immediately conjures two even larger boulders and hurls them side by side. Daren advances at a steady march, sweeping his blade in a reverse cut that swallows both masses, adding two more rotating marbles to the humming orbit around his blade.

"What's the matter, Talmak?" Daren's voice drops low, eyes fixed on his opponent as he closes the distance. "Weren't you going to punish me for my insolence?"

"Sage Talmak!" Nolderan's shout cuts across the yard from where he squares off with Hadrik. "His sword absorbs conjured elements! Use natural bedrock—he can't absorb raw earth fast enough!"

Daren's jaw clenches at his old master's shout, but his stride never falters.

"Oh, so that's how it is..." Talmak's hands drop toward the ground, mana surging into the bedrock.

Before the earth can tear free, Daren whips his sword in a vicious downward slash, hurling all four orbiting marbles straight at the sage.

Mid-flight, the stones expand back to their full, crushing mass. Talmak aborts his ground cast and heaves up a massive stone barrier, but the barrage batters through the center. One boulder punches past the crumbling defense and slams directly into Talmak's chest, knocking him flat on his back.

"Don't let him close the distance!" Nolderan roars. "His blade can sever your link to the magical plane!"

Daren sprints forward, broadsword raised to strike.

From flat on his back, Talmak slams his open palm into the dirt.

A monstrous tremor detonates through the ground. The shockwave flings everyone off their feet as the compound bedrock fractures into webbed crevices. Talmak heaves himself onto a fresh stone slab and shoots twenty feet into the air as the ground tears open below us.

"Damn it, he's cheating again!" I scramble to brace myself on the buckling dirt.

"I think we may be having some bigger problems to deal with, at the moment," Daren grunts, struggling to find purchase in full plate.

The fractures tear wide, the earth shearing in two to reveal a black, bottomless chasm beneath our boots. The ground gives way completely, dropping all of us into the abyss.

choice("Continue", B2-Ch10b-Shocked, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10b-Shocked)


ID: B2-Ch10b-Insult
TEXT:

 "Don't let the sage's imposing physique intimidate you, Daren!" I call out. "If you look closely, you can see that he's trembling with fear!"

"As soon as I'm done with the healer, you are next, boy," Talmak spits. "Prepare yourself."

Talmak thrusts both hands forward. Two massive boulders, each twice Daren's height, tear through the air with concussive force.

